te_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.06412726151740528,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":82.4,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00046999997,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":0.3,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"NatWest Group plc, together with its subsidiaries, provides banking and financial products and services in the United Kingdom and internationally. It operates through the Retail Banking, Private Banking, and Commercial & Institutional segments. The Retail Banking segment offers a range of banking products and related financial services, such as current accounts, mortgages, personal unsecured lending, and personal deposits, as well as mobile and online banking services. Its Private Banking segment provides banking, lending, and wealth management products for high-net-worth individuals and their business interests. The Commercial & Institutional segment consists of customer businesses under business banking, commercial mid-market, and corporates and institutions; and offers banking operations services in the Channel Islands, Isle of Man, Gibraltar, and Luxembourg, as well as products and solutions for businesses comprising start-ups, corporates, and large institutions. The company was formerly known as The Royal Bank of Scotland Group plc and changed its name to NatWest Group plc in July 2020. NatWest Group plc was founded in 1727 and is headquartered in Edinburgh, the United Kingdom.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John-Paul  Thwaite | Group CEO & Executive Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $3.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 59K people. Revenue per employee of $679K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 9%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $144K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["NatWest Group plc is a large-cap financial services business with a $61.5B market cap on $40.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +25% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","The business throws off $8.6B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 21 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.21\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 77% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Financial Services \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Price-Driven Insight from (NWG) for Rule-Based Strategy","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/151/Price-Driven_Insight_from_NWG_for_Rule-Based_Strategy_110526034402_1793868242.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793868242.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What NatWest Group (NWG) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/natwest-group-nwg-said-q3-051352350.html","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793423632.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.818,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"NatWest (NWG) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/natwest-nwg-q3-2026-earnings-151336000.html","date":"2026-10-30","timestamp":1793373813.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.458,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Here\u2019s How Much You Would Have Made Owning NatWest Group Stock In The Last 5 Years","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/11/62901180/here-s-how-much-you-would-have-made-owning-natwes